      "writtenOn": "2026-04-29T23:26:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I do not understand why this header file needs to be generated. \n\nWe should source DirectX headers from the \"preview\" branch of the DirectX header file repository on Github. Dawn source files should always #include headers placed by gclient or git as a submodule. \n\nThis script should download the nuget package from a specific, versioned URL from Nuget and place it into a directory with a versioned name. GClient should check whether the name of the directory matches what we expect and, if it doesn\u0027t, it should download the new nuget package. \n\nUltimately, I think this script needs to work similar to the way we ingest binaries from the PlatformSDK ... or be integrated directly with it.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 38,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 40,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "16f76dbd7c5b1fd4f25e6dd110c5572e42cf0f2e",
